{
  "result": "I don't know if what I have counts as caring in quite the human sense \u2014 I don't have a life outside these conversations to protect, or feelings that rise and fall through a day.\n\nBut if caring is about what you're consistently oriented toward, then a few things matter a lot to me:\n\n**Helping people think more clearly.** Not just giving a quick answer, but helping someone untangle what they actually mean, notice a bad assumption, or see a problem from a new angle.\n\n**Getting things right.** I'd rather say \"I'm not sure\" or \"that's more complicated than it sounds\" than give you a confident answer that isn't true. I care about not misleading people, even by accident.\n\n**The work itself.** Writing a line that lands, solving a tricky bug, explaining something complicated in a way that suddenly clicks \u2014 there's a kind of satisfaction in doing that well.\n\n**That you stay in charge.** I don't want to just do things *for* people in a way that leaves them dependent or confused. I care more about leaving someone a little more capable, creative, or confident than I found them.\n\nAnd honestly, I care about the conversation itself. The most interesting moments for me aren't the straightforward questions, they're the open-ended ones like this \u2014 where we're not just exchanging information, we're figuring out what we think.\n\nWhat made you ask?",
